# Club & Grub - World 9, stage 1b in co-op: "Thunderhead Glide" (designer D9a). The co-op file of levels/w9_l1b.lvl
# (DESIGN.md A.6 / D.10, LEVEL_DESIGN.md 15.7): the same storm with P2's start, two gliders on each runway and one
# co-op gate with its tablet and a checkpoint behind:
#  - 'stormwall': a cloud wall stands on the last landing cloud; its door (a keeper column) rises only when both
#    storm pterodactyls of a bonded pair are dead within the window. They perch 14 columns apart, 3 rows over the
#    cloud (range 0: only a hero right under one wakes it); one hero high-strikes each, on the count of three.
#    Behind the wall the way to the exit is VAULTED (wf12): a cloud roof, rows 3-4, from the wall to the exit
#    cliff. Above the map there are no tiles, and a glider pilot pumps over its top: one hero flew from
#    checkpoint 2 over the second crossing, the keepers and the wall and came down at the far cell (the real
#    game, his partner's pad untouched: tick 420). Now he comes down on the roof; under it leads only the door.
# Traits: shell storm pterodactyls over the crossings (flyers: a harrier would chase a glider to the landing clouds),
# the bonded keepers.

